From: Josef Holzmayr <jester@theyoctojester.info>
Date: Thu, 19 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] raspberrypi: route emmc2 dma-ranges vc-fixup to the real node

On Raspberry Pi 4 the GPU firmware rewrites the emmc2 bus' dma-ranges
property per SoC revision in the device tree it loads, and barebox
forwards that value from the VideoCore fdt into the kernel tree via
register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/emmc2bus", "dma-ranges").

The forward is hardcoded to the path "/emmc2bus", which is the node name
used by the downstream Raspberry Pi kernel dtb (and hence by the VC fdt).
barebox' own, mainline-derived device tree names the same node
"/emmc2-bus@fe000000" (label/alias "emmc2bus"). of_create_node() in the
fixup therefore does not find the controller's bus node by that path and
instead creates a brand new, empty "/emmc2bus" node, writing the
firmware's dma-ranges there. The real emmc2 controller keeps the
compile-time default dma-ranges.

On boards whose SoC revision needs different DMA constraints than the
default, Linux then drives emmc2 DMA into the wrong address window and
the SD card fails to initialise: "mmc1: ADMA error" / "error -5", or,
with ADMA masked, garbage data reads ("unrecognised SCR structure").

Resolve the destination node through the "emmc2bus" alias (defined by
both the VC fdt and barebox' tree) when supplied, so the firmware value
lands on the actual controller bus node regardless of its path. The
existing path-based behaviour is kept for fixups that pass no alias.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Josef Holzmayr <jester@theyoctojester.info>
---
 arch/arm/boards/raspberry-pi/rpi-common.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boards/raspberry-pi/rpi-common.c
+++ b/arch/arm/boards/raspberry-pi/rpi-common.c
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@
 struct rpi_property_fixup_data {
     const struct device_node* vc_node;
     const char *propname;
+    const char *dest_alias;
 };

 static void rpi_set_usbethaddr(void)
@@ -313,7 +314,20 @@
 	struct device_node *node;
 	struct property *prop;

-	node = of_create_node(root, fixup->vc_node->full_name);
+	/*
+	 * The VideoCore fdt and barebox' internal device tree may name the
+	 * same node differently (the emmc2 bus is "/emmc2bus" in the vc fdt
+	 * but "/emmc2-bus@fe000000" in the mainline-derived barebox dts).
+	 * When a destination alias is supplied, resolve the target through it
+	 * so the property lands on the real node rather than a freshly created
+	 * phantom one; fall back to the literal vc path otherwise.
+	 */
+	if (fixup->dest_alias)
+		node = of_find_node_by_alias(root, fixup->dest_alias);
+	else
+		node = NULL;
+	if (!node)
+		node = of_create_node(root, fixup->vc_node->full_name);
 	if (!node)
 		return -ENOMEM;

@@ -326,7 +340,8 @@
 }

 static int register_vc_property_fixup(struct device_node *root,
-						 const char *path, const char *propname)
+						 const char *path, const char *propname,
+						 const char *dest_alias)
 {
 	struct device_node *node, *tmp;
 	struct rpi_property_fixup_data* fixup_data;
@@ -338,6 +353,7 @@
 		fixup_data = xzalloc(sizeof(*fixup_data));
 		fixup_data->vc_node = tmp;
 		fixup_data->propname = xstrdup(propname);
+		fixup_data->dest_alias = dest_alias ? xstrdup(dest_alias) : NULL;

 		of_register_fixup(rpi_vc_fdt_fixup_property, fixup_data);
 	} else {
@@ -373,10 +389,10 @@

 	register_vc_fixup(root, "/system");
 	register_vc_fixup(root, "/axi");
-	register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/reserved-memory/nvram@0", "reg");
-	register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/reserved-memory/nvram@0", "status");
+	register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/reserved-memory/nvram@0", "reg", NULL);
+	register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/reserved-memory/nvram@0", "status", NULL);
 	register_vc_fixup(root, "/hat");
-	register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/emmc2bus", "dma-ranges");
+	register_vc_property_fixup(root, "/emmc2bus", "dma-ranges", "emmc2bus");
 	register_vc_fixup(root, "/chosen/bootloader");
 	chosen = register_vc_fixup(root, "/chosen");
 	if (!chosen) {
